{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-10-20_a2026-q3ex991earningsrelea.htm, sha256 7c09c3083cfe77c8a9adc825f1d61383b9cc6648771794281498f6d524a55b4d.\nEX-99.1 2 a2026-q3ex991earningsrelea.htm EX-99.1\nExhibit 99.1\nNews Release\nWeatherford Announces Third Quarter 2026 Results \u2022Third quarter revenue of $1,143 million increased 3% sequentially \u2022Third quarter operating income of $153 million increased 43% sequentially \u2022Third quarter net income of $120 million increased 208% sequentially; net income margin of 10.5% \u2022Third quarter adjusted EBITDA* of $254 million increased 14% sequentially; adjusted EBITDA margin* of 22.2% increased 204 basis points sequentially \u2022Third quarter cash provided by operating activities of $192 million and adjusted free cash flow* of $155 million \u2022Shareholder return of $47 million for the quarter, which included dividend payments of $19 million and share repurchases of $28 million \u2022Completed the acquisition of NCS Multistage Holdings, Inc. (\u201cNCS Multistage\u201d) in a stock-and-cash transaction, strengthening Weatherford\u2019s completions portfolio and expanding capabilities in reservoir diagnostics and well performance solutions \u2022Secured shareholder approval for the redomestication to Delaware, a strategic initiative expected to generate approximately $20 million to $30 million of annual cash savings beginning in 2027, subject to previously disclosed regulatory and court approvals \u2022Subsequent to quarter end, issued notice to redeem all of 8.625% Senior Notes due 2030 in an aggregate principal amount of $236 million, further improving gross leverage* and enhancing future adjusted free cash flow conversion* \u2022Equinor awarded Weatherford a two-year extension and a new offshore completions award, across several strategic frame agreements to provide its integrated completions portfolio for the Statfjord and Oseberg licenses on the Norwegian Continental Shelf\n*Non-GAAP - refer to the section titled Non-GAAP Financial Measures Defined and GAAP to Non-GAAP Financial Measures Reconciled\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "Houston, October 20, 2026 \u2013 Weatherford International plc (NASDAQ: WFRD) (\u201cWeatherford\u201d or the \u201cCompany\u201d) announced today its results for the third quarter of 2026. Revenues for the third quarter of 2026 were $1,143 million, an increase of 3% sequentially and a decrease of 7% year-over-year. Operating income in the third quarter of 2026 was $153 million, an increase of 43% sequentially and a decrease of 14% year-over-year. Net income in the third quarter of 2026 was $120 million, with a 10.5% margin, an increase of 208%, or 697 basis points, sequentially, and an increase of 48%, or 392 basis points, year-over-year. Adjusted EBITDA* was $254 million, with a 22.2% margin*, an increase of 14% or 204 basis points, sequentially, and a decrease of 6% but an expansion of 39 basis points, year-over-year. Basic income per share in the third quarter of 2026 was $1.66, an increase of 200% sequentially and an increase of 47% year-over-year. Diluted income per share in the third quarter of 2026 was $1.66, an increase of 199% sequentially and an increase of 48% year-over-year. Third quarter 2026 cash flows provided by operating activities were $192 million, an increase of 10% sequentially and an increase of 39% year-over-year. Adjusted free cash flow* was $155 million, an increase of 12% sequentially and an increase of 57% year-over-year. Capital expenditures were $45 million in the third quarter of 2026, an increase of 7% sequentially and an increase of 2% year-over-year. Girish Saligram, President and Chief Executive Officer, commented, \u201cThe One Weatherford team delivered an excellent third quarter, with adjusted EBITDA margin* expanding 204 basis points sequentially to 22.2% and adjusted free cash flow* of $155 million. Even as conflict related operational disruptions in the Middle East weighed on activity levels, the strength of our diversified portfolio, disciplined cost management, and outstanding execution across the organization drove margin expansion and strong cash generation. These results demonstrate the durability of our operating model, agility to pivot in any phase of the cycle, and the earnings potential of the business as activity recovers. We also made significant progress on our strategic priorities during the quarter. The closing of the NCS Multistage acquisition strengthens our completions portfolio, broadens our technology capabilities, and positions us to realize meaningful cost and commercial synergies. We further enhanced our capital structure by issuing a notice to redeem the remaining $236 million principal amount of our 2030 Senior Notes, reducing future interest expense. Shareholders approved our proposed redomestication to Delaware, an important step toward a simpler, more efficient corporate structure and improved free cash flow generation. Finally, our Enterprise Resource Planning (\u201cERP\u201d) transformation remains on track, with our first major application launching very smoothly in the third quarter, enabling greater process\n"}
{"page": 3, "text": "standardization, simplification, operational efficiency and scalability across the enterprise. We enter the final quarter of the year with strong momentum to springboard into 2027. While the recent events in the Middle East have dampened expectations of a quick recovery, we still see a meaningful ramp in adjusted EBITDA* in the fourth quarter and are increasing our full year adjusted free cash flow* guidance yet again. We see significant market opportunities for growth heading into 2027 and are very well positioned to capitalize on those.\u201d *Non-GAAP - refer to the section titled Non-GAAP Financial Measures Defined and GAAP to Non-GAAP Financial Measures Reconciled 2\nOperational & Commercial Highlights \u2022Equinor awarded Weatherford a two-year extension and a new offshore completions award, across several strategic frame agreements to provide its integrated completions portfolio for the Statfjord and Oseberg licenses on the Norwegian Continental Shelf. \u2022A major operator awarded Weatherford a 46-unit contract for the supply of Progressive Cavity Pumping systems, a hallmark of our Artificial Lift capability, to support well completions in Venezuela. \u2022Eldorado Drilling (formerly known as Vantage Drilling) awarded Weatherford a contract to supply a comprehensive Managed Pressure Drilling (\u201cMPD\u201d) equipment package for a 7th-generation ultra-deepwater drillship for a deepwater drilling campaign offshore Indonesia in water depths of approximately 1,700 meters. \u2022A major operator awarded Weatherford a four-year contract to provide Tubular Running Services (\u201cTRS\u201d) and Intervention Services & Drilling Tools (\u201cISDT\u201d), expanding our support across offshore exploration, development and decommissioning activities in Australia. \u2022A National Oil Company (\u201cNOC\u201d) in South-East Asia awarded Weatherford a three-year deepwater liner hanger contract for conventional and expandable liner systems. \u2022Seplat Energy awarded Weatherford a five-year contract to provide Completions Products and Services, including Gas Lift Solutions, for its shallow offshore operations in Nigeria. \u2022Brunei Shell Petroleum awarded Weatherford a five-year contract extension for Thru-Tubing Services which covers the delivery of Weatherford\u2019s thru-tubing portfolio across onshore and offshore wells in Brunei, reinforcing a long-standing partnership focused on safe, reliable, and efficient well intervention solutions. \u2022A major operator awarded Weatherford a 30-month contract to provide MPD services in Argentina. \u2022Joint Operations (Saudi Arabian Chevron Inc. - Kuwait Gulf Oil Company) awarded Weatherford a four-year contract for ForeSite\u00ae and Cygnet\u00ae software in Kuwait. \u2022Kuwait Oil Company awarded Weatherford a five-year contract to provide Directional Drilling, Measurement While Drilling and Logging While Drilling services. \u2022A major drilling contractor awarded Weatherford a one-year contract to provide integrated services for offshore operations in Mexico.\n3\n"}
{"page": 4, "text": "Technology Highlights \u2022Drilling & Evaluation (\u201cDRE\u201d) \u25e6In Thailand, Weatherford deployed its Magnus SakerTM drilling system across six high-temperature well sections, achieving 100% geological target success through single-run shoe-to-shoe operation. The campaign eliminated an additional drilling assembly trip, saved over 100 operational hours, equivalent to over five rig days, and delivered significant customer savings while exceeding the operator\u2019s drilling performance target. \u25e6In the United Kingdom (\u201cUK\u201d), Weatherford completed the first deployment of its Dual Advanced Kickover Tool technology to replace multiple gas-lift valves in a highly deviated offshore well. The solution completed the work in two intervention runs rather than the four typically required, reducing intervention runs by half, saving rig time and reducing personnel exposure at the wellsite.\n\u2022Well Construction and Completions (\u201cWCC\u201d) \u25e6With our acquisition of NCS Multistage, we now bring into our portfolio a differentiated completions technology platform that has surpassed 500,000 frac stages completed since 2009. During the quarter, we secured a Deepwater Gulf of America award for its frac sleeves and service tools following four years of collaborative development with a major international operator. The award expands our footprint into the offshore market, creates a platform for future growth, and highlights the potential to leverage these technologies across a broader range of completion applications. \u25e6In Saudi Arabia, Weatherford deployed a three-stage DV (\u201cDifferential Valve\u201d) Tool for the cementing of a 9-5/8\u201d casing string for Aramco. An open hole annulus casing packer enabled isolation, allowing higher-density fluids in subsequent stages, while staged tools restored internal gas tight integrity, and a V0-rated packer secured the casing-to-casing annulus, supporting an optimized cement program and long-term well integrity. \u25e6In Malaysia, Weatherford completed the first Mature Asset Rejuvenation by Surveillance System (\u201cMARS\u201d) deployment of its kind in Asia for Petronas to evaluate a gas-lift well where a restricted internal diameter prevented the use of conventional tools. The technology completed a full diagnostic survey and accurately identified the leak location, enabling multi-point gas-lift injection diagnosis while avoiding alternative intervention methods.\n4\n"}
{"page": 5, "text": "\u2022Production and Intervention (\u201cPRI\u201d) \u25e6In the U.S., Weatherford completed the first commercial installation of its ForeSite\u00ae Power Regenerative System Retrofit on an existing rod-lift well. The system captures and reuses energy generated during each pumping cycle, delivering over 50% in energy savings while lowering operating costs and emissions without requiring replacement of the installed drive. \u25e6In Colombia, Weatherford completed the world\u2019s first deployment of its SandSureTM XT sand consolidation technology to control sand production without conventional downhole screens. The solution consolidated the sand in place, reducing intervention requirements and lifecycle costs while preserving production performance and improving long-term well reliability.\n5\nCorporate Treasury Debt repayment: On October 20, 2026, Weatherford issued a notice to redeem all of its 8.625% Senior Notes due 2030 (the \u201c2030 Senior Notes\u201d) in an aggregate principal amount of $236 million. The 2030 Senior Notes will be redeemed at 100% of their principal amount, plus accrued and unpaid interest to and including the redemption date of October 30, 2026. The redemption is expected to be funded using cash on hand and is expected to reduce annualized cash interest expense by approximately $20 million. This disclosure does not constitute a notice of redemption with respect to the 2030 Senior Notes. Credit Ratings: During the third quarter of 2026, Fitch Ratings and S&P Global Ratings revised their outlook on Weatherford to \u2018Positive Outlook\u2019 from \u2018Stable Outlook\u2019, while affirming the Company\u2019s \u2018BB\u2019 credit rating. Moody\u2019s affirmed its \u2018Ba2\u2019 rating with a \u2018Positive Outlook\u2019. Despite the challenging conditions in the Middle East, these actions recognize Weatherford\u2019s continued improvement in credit profile, supported by a stronger balance sheet, enhanced financial flexibility, and prudent capital allocation.\nShareholder Return During the third quarter of 2026, Weatherford paid dividends of $19 million and repurchased shares for $28 million, resulting in a total shareholder return of $47 million. During the nine months ended September 30, 2026, Weatherford paid dividends of $59 million and repurchased shares for approximately $54 million, resulting in a total shareholder return of $113 million. On October 15, 2026, our Board declared a cash dividend of $0.275 per share of the Company\u2019s ordinary shares. The dividend is payable on December 3, 2026, to shareholders of record as of November 6, 2026.\n"}
{"page": 6, "text": "Other Events The shareholders of Weatherford approved all proposals required to effect the Company\u2019s updated plan of redomestication from Ireland to Delaware, including approval at both the Scheme Meeting and Extraordinary General Meeting. The redomestication remains subject to previously disclosed closing conditions, including sanction by the Irish High Court. Subject to satisfaction of those conditions, the Company expects the transition to become effective during the fourth quarter of 2026. The redomestication shareholder vote marks a significant milestone in Weatherford\u2019s continued transformation and advances the Company\u2019s plan to establish a corporate structure better aligned with its global operations, long-term strategy, and shareholder base. This transaction is expected to generate $20 million to $30 million in annual cash savings beginning in 2027, which we believe is an important contributor to continued improvement in adjusted free cash flow conversion. 6\nResults by Reportable Segment Drilling and Evaluation (\u201cDRE\u201d)\nThree Months Ended Variance\n($ in Millions) Sep 30, 2026 Jun 30, 2026 Sep 30, 2025 Seq. YoY\nRevenue $ 331 $ 291 $ 346 14 % (4) %\nSegment Adjusted EBITDA $ 90 $ 58 $ 83 55 % 8 %\nSegment Adj EBITDA Margin 27.2 % 19.9 % 24.0 % 726 bps 320 bps\nThird quarter 2026 DRE revenue of $331 million increased by $40 million, or 14% sequentially, primarily from higher MPD and Drilling Services activity in Latin America and higher MPD and Wireline activity in the Middle East/North Africa/Asia, partly offset by lower MPD activity in Europe/Sub-Sahara Africa/Russia. Year-over-year DRE revenue decreased by $15 million, or 4%, primarily from lower Wireline and Drilling-related Services activity, partly offset by higher MPD activity in Latin America. Third quarter 2026 DRE segment adjusted EBITDA of $90 million increased by $32 million, or 55% sequentially, primarily from higher MPD and Drilling Services activity and strong fall through in the Middle East/North Africa/Asia and Latin America, partly offset by lower fall through in North America. Year-over-year DRE segment adjusted EBITDA increased by $7 million, or 8%, primarily from higher fall through in the Middle East/North Africa/Asia and Europe/Sub-Sahara Africa/Russia, partly offset by lower activity and fall through in North America. Well Construction and Completions (\u201cWCC\u201d)\nThree Months Ended Variance\n($ in Millions) Sep 30, 2026 Jun 30, 2026 Sep 30, 2025 Seq. YoY\nRevenue $ 450 $ 433 $ 468 4 % (4) %\nSegment Adjusted EBITDA $ 100 $ 107 $ 125 (7) % (20) %\nSegment Adj EBITDA Margin 22.2 % 24.7 % 26.7 % (249) bps (449) bps\n"}
{"page": 7, "text": "Third quarter 2026 WCC revenue of $450 million increased by $17 million, or 4% sequentially, primarily from higher Completions activity in North America and higher Liner Hangers activity in the Middle East/North Africa/Asia, partly offset by lower Completions activity in Latin America. Year-over-year, WCC revenues decreased by $18 million, or 4%, primarily from lower activity in Middle East/North Africa/Asia, partly offset by higher Completions activity in North America and Latin America. Third quarter 2026 WCC segment adjusted EBITDA of $100 million decreased by $7 million, or 7% sequentially, primarily from lower fall through in North America and lower activity in Europe/Sub-Sahara Africa/Russia, partly offset by higher TRS and Completions activity and fall through in the Middle East/North Africa/Asia. Year-over-year WCC segment adjusted EBITDA decreased by $25 million, or 20%, primarily from lower fall through in North America, partly offset by higher Completions and Cementation Products activity and fall through in Latin America. 7\nProduction and Intervention (\u201cPRI\u201d)\nThree Months Ended Variance\n($ in Millions) Sep 30, 2026 Jun 30, 2026 Sep 30, 2025 Seq. YoY\nRevenue $ 314 $ 316 $ 326 (1) % (4) %\nSegment Adjusted EBITDA $ 73 $ 70 $ 59 4 % 24 %\nSegment Adj EBITDA Margin 23.2 % 22.2 % 18.1 % 110 bps 515 bps\nThird quarter 2026 PRI revenue of $314 million decreased by $2 million, or 1% sequentially, primarily from lower international Pressure Pumping activity, partly offset by higher Artificial Lift and Subsea Intervention activity in Latin America. Year-over-year PRI revenue decreased by $12 million, or 4%, primarily from lower ISDT and Artificial Lift activity in North America and lower Pressure Pumping and ISDT activity in Latin America, partly offset by higher ISDT and Pressure Pumping activity in Europe/Sub-Sahara Africa/Russia. Third quarter 2026 PRI segment adjusted EBITDA of $73 million increased by $3 million, or 4%, sequentially, primarily from higher international Pressure Pumping fall through and higher ISDT and Digital Solutions activity and fall through in the Middle East/North Africa/Asia, partly offset by lower fall through in North America. Year-over-year PRI segment adjusted EBITDA increased by $14 million, or 24% primarily from higher activity and fall through in Europe/Sub-Sahara Africa/Russia, and higher fall through in the Middle East/North Africa/Asia, partly offset by lower ISDT and Pressure Pumping activity in Latin America. Revenue by Geography\nThree Months Ended Variance\n($ in Millions) Sep 30, 2026 Jun 30, 2026 Sep 30, 2025 Seq. YoY\nNorth America $ 236 $ 205 $ 243 15 % (3) %\nInternational $ 907 $ 900 $ 989 1 % (8) %\nLatin America 225 197 214 14 % 5 %\nMiddle East/North Africa/Asia 447 446 533 \u2014 % (16) %\nEurope/Sub-Sahara Africa/Russia 235 257 242 (9) % (3) %\nTotal Revenue $ 1,143 $ 1,105 $ 1,232 3 % (7) %\n"}
{"page": 8, "text": "North America Third quarter 2026 North America revenue of $236 million increased by $31 million, or 15%, sequentially, primarily from higher activity across all reported segments, especially Completions activity in U.S. Land and Canada Land, partly offset by lower Completions activity in U.S. offshore. Year-over-year, North America revenue decreased by $7 million, or 3%, primarily from lower activity in ISDT and Artificial Lift product lines, especially in U.S. Land, partly offset by higher Completions activity. 8\nInternational Third quarter 2026 international revenue of $907 million increased by $7 million, or 1% sequentially and decreased by $82 million, or 8% year-over-year. Third quarter 2026 Latin America revenue of $225 million increased by $28 million, or 14% sequentially, primarily from higher Drilling-related Services and Integrated Services & Projects (\u201cISP\u201d) activity in Mexico and higher MPD activity in the Caribbean, partly offset by lower Completions and Pressure Pumping activity. Year-over-year, Latin America revenue increased by $11 million, or 5%, primarily from higher MPD activity in the Caribbean and higher Completions activity, partly offset by lower Drilling-related Services activity in Argentina and Mexico. Third quarter 2026 Middle East/North Africa/Asia revenue of $447 million was largely flat sequentially, as lower ISP activity was partly offset by higher MPD and Liner Hangers activity. Year-over-year, the Middle East/North Africa/Asia revenue decreased by $86 million, or 16%, primarily from subdued activity on account of heightened geopolitical tensions partly offset by higher Cementation Products activity. Third quarter 2026 Europe/Sub-Sahara Africa/Russia revenue of $235 million decreased by $22 million, or 9% sequentially, primarily from lower activity across the reported segments, partly offset by higher Wireline activity in Europe. Year-over-year, Europe/Sub-Sahara Africa/Russia revenue decreased by $7 million, or 3%, primarily from lower Wireline and Liner Hangers activity, partly offset by higher activity in the PRI segment.\n9\n"}
{"page": 9, "text": "About Weatherford Weatherford is a global energy services company that helps customers drill smarter, complete wells more effectively, and maximize production across the entire well lifecycle. With a differentiated portfolio of market-leading solutions, integrated technologies, and a broad global customer footprint across six continents, we blend advanced engineering, digital intelligence, and world-class field expertise to reduce risk, improve performance, and maximize the value of customer assets. Together, we elevate every operation, delivering stronger wells, sharper decisions, and better energy for the world. Visit weatherford.com for more information and connect with us on social media. Conference Call Details Weatherford will host a conference call on Wednesday, October 21, 2026, to discuss the Company\u2019s results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2026. The conference call will begin at 8:30 a.m. Eastern Time (7:30 a.m. Central Time). Listeners are encouraged to download the accompanying presentation slides which will be available in the investor relations section of the Company\u2019s website. Listeners can participate in the conference call via a live webcast at https://www.weatherford.com/investor-relations/investor-news-and-events/events/ or by dialing +1 877-328-5344 (within the U.S.) or +1 412-902-6762 (outside of the U.S.) and asking for the Weatherford conference call. Participants should log in or dial in approximately 10 minutes prior to the start of the call. A telephonic replay of the conference call will be available until November 4, 2026, at 5:00 p.m. Eastern Time. To access the replay, please dial +1 855-669-9658 (within the U.S.) or +1 412-317-0088 (outside of the U.S.) and reference conference number 2939769. A replay and transcript of the earnings call will also be available in the investor relations section of the Company\u2019s website. Contacts For Investors: Luke Lemoine Senior Vice President, Corporate Development & Investor Relations +1 713-836-7777 investor.relations@weatherford.com\nFor Media: Kelley Hughes Vice President, Communications, Marketing & Sustainability media@weatherford.com\n10\n"}
